Through human review, it seemed that some questions were failing because it did not get the correct chunk id but was getting a number +-5 to chunk id. Considering overlap, re reviewed all failed questions. 
Review Criteria:

* How clear and specific the question was
* Whether it clearly mentioned identifiable details (such as a report, case, program, agency, year, or topic)
* Whether the gold passage fully supported the reference answer
* Whether any retrieved content included enough evidence to support the answer
* Whether any valid supporting passages were missing from the gold annotations
* Whether the issue was truly a retrieval failure

Each case was then placed into one of the following categories:

* `TRUE_RETRIEVAL_FAILURE`
* `INCOMPLETE_GOLD_LABEL`
* `AMBIGUOUS_QUESTION`
* `BAD_REFERENCE_OR_GOLD_SPAN`
* `OTHER`

Failure review summary:
  AMBIGUOUS_QUESTION           6
  INCOMPLETE_GOLD_LABEL        6
  TRUE_RETRIEVAL_FAILURE       38

LLM vague-question flags: 6
Fast vagueness flags: 10
Fast/LLM disagreements: 6

Fix : 
- Rephrased Ambigious questions.
- Ran review criteria on those specific questions and tweaked until passed.
- Reran evaluate.py on fixed questions.
- Manually replaced caches.
- Reevaluated metrics.

